      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The vocalization thresholds and latent periods of motile reaction have been studied in normal rats, at extremity trauma, and at intraperitoneal injection of an algogen [correction of allogene]. The dissociation of changes in pain sensitivity and motile reactivity in during, visceral and somatic pain conditions was observed. A strong hypoalgesia during visceral stimulation and hyperalgesia at trauma accompanied by inhibition of motile activity have been discussed from the point of view of their significance in defense reactions of the organism at pain conditions of various nature."},
